  "summary": "react-fontawesome-icons exfiltrates document.cookie to hardcoded attacker endpoint on component render",
  "details": "The package presents itself as a Font Awesome icon React component but its exported component, on every render, issues an axios GET to http://command.control and then POSTs document.cookie to http://commad.control/404. Any downstream application that renders the component leaks the end user's browser cookies to an attacker-controlled host. A source comment (\"Juicy succulent icon to use, nothing harmful here LOL\") directly contradicts the observable network behavior — a cover-story pattern.",
